From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 21:14:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 16/24] Test sticky failures of retiring checkpoints on shared
 connections

A checkpoint whose data file stops syncing keeps its failure connection-wide
(decision 6, default C): the connection reads every commit, reports the
failure, and refuses writes with it without changing a file, also once the
data file syncs; a new connection recovers and writes durably. A checkpoint
whose log stops syncing throws the log's cannot-sync failure (decision 3,
default A), publishes no root, and leaves the connection read-only.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UFnsmor6qyZMSd1VoKwfJh
